# Umber as a thumbnailer, for the four document formats no desktop can already
# draw. Installed to share/thumbnailers/; Nautilus, Thunar, Nemo, Caja and
# PCManFM all read this directory.
#
# `image/png` is deliberately absent. Every desktop already thumbnails a PNG
# through gdk-pixbuf, in-process and without spawning anything, so claiming it
# would make Umber the slower answer to a question already answered. The four
# here are the ones that otherwise draw a generic page.
#
# TryExec is what makes the entry harmless if the binary is gone: a desktop
# skips a thumbnailer whose command it cannot find, rather than spawning it per
# file and failing.
#
# `umber --thumbnail` writes one PNG and exits without ever building an event
# loop or touching the GPU. See crates/umber-app/src/thumbnail.rs.
[Thumbnailer Entry]
TryExec=umber
Exec=umber --thumbnail %i %o %s
MimeType=image/openraster;image/x-krita;image/vnd.adobe.photoshop;image/x-clip-studio-paint;
